    "text": {
     "en": "In the 6th to 10th centuries many regional kingdoms rose, land grants to priests and officials grew, temples became centres of wealth and learning, and new languages and arts developed.\nArabs reached Sindh in 712 CE and Turkic and other raiders later entered from the north-west. Trade with West and South-East Asia grew.\nScholars like Aryabhata's followers, poets and temple artists enriched life. Universities at Nalanda attracted students from abroad."
    }
